   "text": "Ontario Tech University (Undergraduate Arts Courses) - QS Apply\nSkip to main content\nHOMEPAGE\nAPPLICATIONS\nNOTIFICATIONS\nEK\nOntario Tech University (Undergraduate Arts Courses)\nSummary\nDegrees and Programs\nStudent Testimonials\nCommission\nViewer Access\nAny user can see this institution.\nDescription\nModern and forwarding-thinking, Ontario Tech University advances the discovery and application of knowledge to accelerate economic growth, regional development and social innovation. We inspire and equip our students and graduates to make a positive impact in a tech-focused world.We adapt to the ever-changing educational landscape by experimenting with the most effective ways to deliver flexible and dynamic learning, giving more choices to more people. By offering a range of credentials and experiential learning opportunities, and sparking entrepreneurship activities, we provide learner-centred educational options. Our students enjoy a stimulating campus life experience that includes hundreds of clubs, cultural and community events, recreational opportunities and a growing varsity athletics program featuring basketball, badminton, curling, dance, golf, hockey, rowing, soccer, and women’s lacrosse. In addition to excellence in teaching, we offer our students experiential learning opportunities through internships, co-ops, practicums, research projects and more. In fact, 85 percent of upper-year undergraduate students participate in experiential learning.  collaborate with industry, community, government and academic organizations, bringing them together with our researchers and students to uncover innovative solutions for our partners’ most pressing problems. The home to more than 80 specialized research laboratories and facilities, we’re committed to attracting passionate and capable scholars to our high-tech campus.\nTimestamps\nUpdated\n04/06/2026 08:42\nby Eston Dalmeida\nCreated\n06/06/2023 10:36\nby Data Migration\nType\nUniversity\nCountry\nCanada\nYearly Fees\nMax: CA$39,000.00\nMin: CA$29,000.00\nInternational Students\nPercentage of International Students\n12%\n1,200 of 10,000 Total Students\nOverview\nBasic Details\nInstitution Details\nOwnership\nPublic\nProvider\nDirect QS\nFounded Year\n2002\nCampus(es)\nOshawa\nCountry\nCanada\nExcluded Countries\nNA\nPREMIUM INSTITUTION\n No\nContract Start Date\n27/05/2025\nContract End Date\n26/05/2027\nContract Entity\nQSSA Ltd\nContract Status\nActive\nContract Document Link(s)\nN/A\nImages\nImages\nAdditional Details\nAccommodation Details\nhttps://ontariotechu.ca/current-students/campus-services/housing-options/on-campus.php\nScholarship Offered\nhttps://studentlife.ontariotechu.ca/current-students/accessibility/financial-support/index.php\nYouTube Video Link(s)\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HXz08CyFE7E\nInternship Details\nhttps://studentlife.ontariotechu.ca/employers/internships-and-co-ops.php\nAdditional Information\nEligibility review of students shall be conducted by the client after the 20th day of classes.",
